From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 10:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] soc/intel/common/block/acpi/pep: Skip a device without an
 ACPI path

acpi_lpi_get_constraints() counts every enabled PCI device with a
minimum sleep state and writes a three-element package for each, with
acpi_device_path() as the first element. A device that no node of the
DSDT or SSDT names has no path: acpi_device_path() returns NULL,
acpigen_emit_namestring() writes nothing, and the package is declared
three long with two elements. On a Lenovo ThinkCentre M920x (Cannon
Point-H) that is the PCH thermal controller at 00:12.0, enabled and in
the SoC's list of minimum sleep states, which soc_acpi_name() of
Cannon Lake does not name; iasl reports "Initializer list shorter than
declared package length" (remark 2063) on the _DSM of PEPD, and an OS
reading the constraints finds an entry whose device is uninitialized.

Leave such a device out, in the count and in the list, and say so at
DEBUG.
---
 src/soc/intel/common/block/acpi/pep.c | 18 ++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/soc/intel/common/block/acpi/pep.c b/src/soc/intel/common/block/acpi/pep.c
index f2df6fb55af..d4aa6be8801 100644
--- a/src/soc/intel/common/block/acpi/pep.c
+++ b/src/soc/intel/common/block/acpi/pep.c
@@ -173,8 +173,20 @@ static void acpi_lpi_get_constraints(void *unused)
 			if (!dev->enabled || dev->hidden)
 				continue;
 			if (get_min_sleep_state(dev, states_arr, size)
-				!= ACPI_DEVICE_SLEEP_NONE)
-				num_entries++;
+				== ACPI_DEVICE_SLEEP_NONE)
+				continue;
+			/*
+			 * A PCI device without an ACPI node (no device in the
+			 * DSDT or SSDT names it) has no path to constrain: left
+			 * out, or the package below would be declared one entry
+			 * longer than its list.
+			 */
+			if (dev->path.type == DEVICE_PATH_PCI && !acpi_device_path(dev)) {
+				printk(BIOS_DEBUG, "PEPD: no ACPI path for %s, no constraint\n",
+				       dev_path(dev));
+				continue;
+			}
+			num_entries++;
 		}
 	}
 	if (!num_entries) {
@@ -190,6 +202,8 @@ static void acpi_lpi_get_constraints(void *unused)
 			min_sleep_state = get_min_sleep_state(dev, states_arr, size);
 			if (min_sleep_state == ACPI_DEVICE_SLEEP_NONE)
 				continue;
+			if (dev->path.type == DEVICE_PATH_PCI && !acpi_device_path(dev))
+				continue;
 
 			acpigen_write_package(3);
 			{
